WEBVTT

00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:12.413
[groans]

00:00:12.496 --> 00:00:13.914
[sighs]

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:17.293
[snoring]

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.264
We can't just leave
without saying goodbye.

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:38.939
Goodbye, Sis.
It's time for us to make our own destiny.

00:00:39.023 --> 00:00:41.317
And maybe even make our own lunch.

00:00:41.859 --> 00:00:43.569
We may never see you again.

00:01:12.139 --> 00:01:13.307
[yawns]

00:01:13.391 --> 00:01:15.935
[both snoring]

00:01:16.018 --> 00:01:18.104
Huh? [muttering]

00:01:18.187 --> 00:01:20.773
[snoring]

00:01:20.856 --> 00:01:21.941
Did you hear that?

00:01:22.024 --> 00:01:25.945
Huh? Wha-- I-- I don't hear anything.

00:01:26.028 --> 00:01:29.949
Right. It's too quiet.
Nothing's breaking. No one's fighting.

00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:31.826
That can only mean one thing.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:34.829
They're gone. They took all their things.

00:01:34.912 --> 00:01:36.455
They don't have any things.

00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:37.540
[Ellie] Exactly.

00:01:37.623 --> 00:01:40.251
Uh-oh. This is not gonna go well for you.

00:01:40.751 --> 00:01:44.755
Manny, my brothers are out there
in the wild, and it's all your fault.

00:01:44.839 --> 00:01:45.840
What, my fault?

00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:49.427
Well, you did challenge them
to try to survive on their own.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:51.595
In effect, sending them to their doom.

00:01:51.679 --> 00:01:52.763
[Manny] Thanks, Sid.

00:01:52.847 --> 00:01:55.391
Anytime, buddy. I always got your back.

00:01:55.474 --> 00:01:56.600
Don't worry, honey.

00:01:56.684 --> 00:02:00.521
If-- If Crash and Eddie get into trouble,
they'll find their way back.

00:02:00.604 --> 00:02:01.814
Find their way back?

00:02:01.897 --> 00:02:04.066
The only thing worse
than their survival skills

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.526
is their sense of direction.

00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:07.737
Mmm. And their math skills
aren't great either.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.405
Come on. We've got to find them.

00:02:12.992 --> 00:02:17.830
[Sid] They also have zero musical talent.
And they're awful at bird calls.

00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:22.626
[Crash and Eddie laughing]

00:02:23.627 --> 00:02:26.714
Dude, being on our own totally rules!

00:02:26.797 --> 00:02:29.967
And we've got nothing to worry about
since we've got nine lives.

00:02:30.051 --> 00:02:33.054
-Oh, come on. Everyone knows that's dogs.
-Oh.

00:02:33.137 --> 00:02:34.764
Well, how many lives do we get?

00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:36.682
I forget. It's either four or eleven.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.185
[grunting]

00:02:40.853 --> 00:02:43.272
[Eddie] Destiny awaits!

00:02:43.356 --> 00:02:45.191
[both scream]

00:02:45.941 --> 00:02:47.360
[both groan]

00:02:47.985 --> 00:02:49.570
[Crash] Destiny hurts.

00:02:55.993 --> 00:02:57.495
[Eddie] Have we been here before?

00:02:57.995 --> 00:03:00.164
[Crash] It does look kinda familiar.

00:03:00.247 --> 00:03:03.125
Wait. Is this the way to the Lost World?

00:03:03.751 --> 00:03:06.462
It's the most exciting place
we've ever been!

00:03:07.004 --> 00:03:10.341
It's also the most dangerous.
Do you think we can find it?

00:03:10.841 --> 00:03:13.010
With our keen sense of direction? [laughs]

00:03:13.678 --> 00:03:16.639
Puh-lease. To the Lost World!

00:03:18.891 --> 00:03:20.059
[Crash] Dead end!

00:03:20.893 --> 00:03:22.269
[Eddie] To the Lost World!

00:03:29.151 --> 00:03:30.194
[slurps]

00:03:38.452 --> 00:03:41.455
[sighs] It's hopeless.
We'll never find it.

00:03:42.498 --> 00:03:43.499
[Crash] Found it!

00:03:47.336 --> 00:03:49.171
[Eddie] Ooh.

00:03:50.423 --> 00:03:53.092
Ellie told us never,
ever to go back in there.

00:04:00.683 --> 00:04:03.602
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:07.773
-To the Lost World!
-To the Lost World!

00:04:07.857 --> 00:04:08.941
[both laughing]

00:04:14.739 --> 00:04:16.115
Whoa!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.412
[Orson in sing-song] I smell mammals.

00:04:22.329 --> 00:04:24.457
[match flickering]

00:04:25.166 --> 00:04:29.337
[roaring, snarling]

00:04:33.758 --> 00:04:34.842
[Orson] Snack time.

00:04:34.925 --> 00:04:36.719
[raptors snarl]

00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:43.976
[sniffing, groans]

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.562
Your breath, dude.
You've gotta brush more.

00:04:47.146 --> 00:04:48.356
[both shudder]

00:04:48.439 --> 00:04:51.359
[gulps] I think I just swallowed
my Adam's apple.

00:04:51.442 --> 00:04:52.860
[both scream]

00:04:55.946 --> 00:04:58.616
[Crash] One of us should give ourselves up
so the other can get away!

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:00.743
[Eddie] Good idea! I volunteer you!

00:05:00.826 --> 00:05:02.620
[both scream]

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:10.628
[sighs] That was close.

00:05:10.711 --> 00:05:14.548
[gasps] Crash,
it's just like I remembered it!

00:05:20.554 --> 00:05:23.766
It always amazes me
there's a whole world down here.

00:05:23.849 --> 00:05:25.142
Right below our feet.

00:05:25.226 --> 00:05:27.645
And a giant spider right above our heads.

00:05:27.728 --> 00:05:29.355
[snarling]

00:05:29.438 --> 00:05:30.606
[both scream]

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.569
[panting]

00:05:41.909 --> 00:05:43.703
We're gonna be goners!

00:05:43.786 --> 00:05:47.206
Yeah! And then
we'll only have three or ten more lives!

00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:48.416
[screams]

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.751
[Crash] You know that whole
"living on our own" thing?

00:05:50.835 --> 00:05:53.212
-[Eddie] Yeah?
-I'm starting to question our judgment!

00:05:53.295 --> 00:05:55.756
Well, this is the perfect time to do it.

00:05:59.051 --> 00:06:01.971
[whooping]

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:07.101
I remember this guy.
He's allergic to possums.

00:06:07.184 --> 00:06:09.061
[sniffs, sneezes]

00:06:09.562 --> 00:06:11.856
[screaming]

00:06:16.485 --> 00:06:18.362
[pterodactyl chirps]

00:06:18.446 --> 00:06:19.739
Hello, boys!

00:06:19.822 --> 00:06:21.282
-Buck!
-Buck?

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.994
That's right! Buck Wild, at your service.

00:06:25.077 --> 00:06:26.412
Our hero!

00:06:26.996 --> 00:06:28.831
The legend of the Lost World!

00:06:28.914 --> 00:06:30.458
The wizard of weasels!

00:06:30.541 --> 00:06:32.043
The yin to my yang!

00:06:32.543 --> 00:06:34.920
Your ways are strange
and mysterious, Buck,

00:06:35.004 --> 00:06:36.213
but mostly strange.

00:06:36.297 --> 00:06:37.506
Thanks for dropping in.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.468
Will the rest of the herd
be falling from the sky too?

00:06:40.551 --> 00:06:43.179
I don't think I can catch the mammoths.
One, maybe.

00:06:43.804 --> 00:06:44.847
[all groan]

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.433
[Buck] Mayday! Mayday!
We're coming in hot!

00:06:49.977 --> 00:06:52.021
-Whoa!
-[snarls]

00:06:52.104 --> 00:06:53.397
[groans]

00:06:54.523 --> 00:06:55.941
[Buck] This is your captain speaking.

00:06:56.025 --> 00:06:59.987
Please keep your whiskers and bottoms
inside the dactyl at all times.

00:07:00.071 --> 00:07:01.614
Whoo-hoo!

00:07:01.697 --> 00:07:03.199
-[chitters]
-[snarls]

00:07:03.282 --> 00:07:04.367
[both gasp]

00:07:07.286 --> 00:07:09.121
-Buck!
-Crack!

